course: dictionary
lesson: 15838
title: Hidden words: undetected
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word undetected is built from parts you may already know. Un- means not, and detect means to find out or notice. So undetected means not found out or not noticed. «The cat crept into the kitchen undetected.» Nobody saw the cat go in.
explain: Check the clues around the word. «The leak went undetected for a whole month.» A leak that lasts a month without anyone spotting it is a leak nobody found. The words for a long time tell you it stayed hidden.
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to test it. «The spy slipped past the guards undetected.» If you put not noticed in place of undetected and it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Un- at the start of a word means not, so undetected means not detected.
fact: «Undetected» means not noticed, found or discovered.
fact: «Undetected» can also mean not found by a test or a machine, as in «The illness went undetected».
fact: Useful phrases: «go undetected», «remain undetected», «slip past undetected».
fact: Tests, alarms and microscopes help find things that would otherwise stay undetected.
exercise: «The thief left the house undetected.» What does undetected mean here? | Full of noise | *Not noticed | Out loud and proud | Very angry
exercise: Find and copy the word that means not found: «The illness went undetected for years.» | illness | years | went | *undetected
exercise: Why are tests and alarms important, as the lesson says? | So that nothing is ever found | Because they are loud and fun | So that leaks can stay undetected for longer | *So that leaks and illnesses do not go undetected for a long time
test: «The mouse ran across the kitchen floor undetected.» What does undetected mean? | *Not noticed by anyone | Very tired | Loudly | Seen by everyone
test: Which phrase means to stay hidden and not be noticed? | *Remain undetected | Shout loudly | Go away | Eat lunch
exam: Ali says the leak went undetected for a month. What does it mean? | Fixed quickly by a plumber | *Not found for a long time | Painted over | Found on the first day
